{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ll inspect the three fixes and their tests, then check how the budgeted reader interacts with `mirror-step` and whether the cursor check covers each served surface. I’ll use the orchestrator’s verified test counts without rerunning suites."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc && nl -ba test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc && nl -ba test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve\n     2\t  \"The FFI export binding: the exporter side of\n     3\t   `docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3 for a machine's served\n     4\t   handles, composed as one binding value with one drive owner.\n     5\t\n     6\t   `dao.stream.remote` stays the generic transport -- its mirror\n     7\t   answers from a plain table and holds nothing between steps -- and\n     8\t   `yin.vm.ucf.remote` stays a lift/lower facade parameterized by a\n     9\t   `serve!` callback. This namespace owns what neither does: the\n    10\t   registry of served handles, the published table the mirror reads,\n    11\t   the channel end and the mirror's own cursor on it, and the\n    12\t   retirement of served identities.\n    13\t\n    14\t   Policy is injected, never decided here. `open!` takes the channel\n    15\t   end and its descriptor, the per-handle surface policy, the capacity\n    16\t   of live exports and the handler authority gate as required options\n    17\t   and refuses an incomplete assembly before anything is published.\n    18\t\n    19\t   The registry is keyed by the live handle's REFERENCE identity\n    20\t   (`identical?`), never by descriptor or value equality: two equal\n    21\t   values are two exports. Each entry records the handle, its minted\n    22\t   served identity, the channel descriptor, the declared surface and\n    23\t   its status. Repeated `serve!` for one live handle returns the one\n    24\t   identity -- `lift-frame` asks for the same handle while minting a\n    25\t   cell and again while lifting its entry. A served identity is never\n    26\t   reused: a retired handle served again gets a new one.\n    27\t\n    28\t   `retire!` is the one retirement transition (lease reclaim, 3b,\n    29\t   calls it too): it removes the identity from the published table\n    30\t   first, so a later remote operation answers not-found, and only then\n    31\t   releases the entry. The binding owns its channel end outright:\n    32\t   `open!` requires the composition to declare it exclusive (no other\n    33\t   reflection or mirror uses it), so `close!` retires every entry and\n    34\t   closes the channel writer, and a remote peer's unresolved appends\n    35\t   end through the transport's own close/loss path as append-unknown.\n    36\t\n    37\t   The binding's state cell is private to the binding value: no\n    38\t   namespace-level registry exists, and the one drive owner that holds\n    39\t   the binding serializes serve!, step, retire! and close!.\"\n    40\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    41\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    42\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t;; =============================================================================\n    46\t;; Assembly\n    47\t;; =============================================================================\n    48\t\n    49\t(def surfaces\n    50\t  \"The surfaces a served entry may declare (`dao.stream.remote.md`\n    51\t   S2.3): the mirror maps cursor and next to :reader, append! to\n    52\t   :writer.\"\n    53\t  #{:reader :writer})\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn- channel-end?\n    57\t  [end]\n    58\t  (and (map? end)\n    59\t       (stream/reader? (:reader end))\n    60\t       (stream/descriptor? (:reader end))\n    61\t       (stream/writer? (:writer end))))\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn- capacity?\n    65\t  [n]\n    66\t  (and (integer? n) (pos? n)))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- codec?\n    70\t  [c]\n    71\t  (and (map? c) (fn? (:encode c)) (fn? (:decode c))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(def ^:private required\n    75\t  \"Each required option, the check its value must pass, and the reason\n    76\t   a present value that fails it is refused with (::malformed unless\n    77\t   named).\"\n    78\t  [[::channel channel-end?]\n    79\t   [::channel-exclusive? true? ::not-exclusive]\n    80\t   [::channel-descriptor stream/valid-descriptor?]\n    81\t   [::surface fn?]\n    82\t   [::admit? fn?]\n    83\t   [::capacity capacity?]\n    84\t   [::step-budget capacity?]])\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\t(def ^:private optional\n    88\t  \"Each optional option and the check its value must pass when given.\"\n    89\t  [[::codec codec?]])\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t(defn- refusals\n    93\t  \"The required options `opts` lacks, and any option it carries\n    94\t   malformed, in order.\"\n    95\t  [opts]\n    96\t  (into []\n    97\t        (concat\n    98\t          (keep (fn [[k ok? reason]]\n    99\t                  (cond\n   100\t                    (not (contains? opts k)) {::option k, ::reason ::missing}\n   101\t                    (not (ok? (get opts k)))\n   102\t                    {::option k, ::reason (or reason ::malformed)}))\n   103\t                required)\n   104\t          (keep (fn [[k ok?]]\n   105\t                  (when (and (contains? opts k) (not (ok? (get opts k))))\n   106\t                    {::option k, ::reason ::malformed}))\n   107\t                optional))))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn binding?\n   111\t  \"True when `b` is a binding `open!` assembled.\"\n   112\t  [b]\n   113\t  (and (map? b) (contains? b ::state)))\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t(defn open!\n   117\t  \"Assemble one export binding from `opts`, or refuse.\n   118\t\n   119\t   Required options, all policy the composition decides:\n   120\t     ::channel            the binding's channel end {:reader r :writer w}:\n   121\t                          r carries remote requests toward this peer,\n   122\t                          w carries answers back\n   123\t     ::channel-exclusive? exactly true: the composition's declaration of\n   124\t                          the binding's ownership contract -- this\n   125\t                          channel end is dedicated to this binding, and\n   126\t                          no other reflection or mirror reads or writes\n   127\t                          it. A handle cannot prove exclusivity, so the\n   128\t                          composition must declare it; anything but\n   129\t                          true refuses as ::not-exclusive. `close!`\n   130\t                          closes the writer on the strength of it\n   131\t     ::channel-descriptor the channel's portable descriptor, stamped on\n   132\t                          every served descriptor\n   133\t     ::surface            handle -> a non-empty subset of #{:reader\n   134\t                          :writer}, or nil to refuse the handle\n   135\t     ::admit?             handle -> truthy when the handler authority\n   136\t                          gate admits exporting it; there is no default\n   137\t                          -- a composition that admits everything says\n   138\t                          so with (constantly true)\n   139\t     ::capacity           the positive bound on live exports\n   140\t     ::step-budget        the positive bound on channel reads one\n   141\t                          `step` makes: the drive pass is bounded\n   142\t\n   143\t   Optional:\n   144\t     ::codec              the channel codec {:encode f :decode f} a\n   145\t                          served reader's cursors must round-trip\n   146\t                          through; `yin.vm.ucf.remote/cursor-codec`\n   147\t                          when absent\n   148\t\n   149\t   Returns the binding, or `{::status ::refused, ::refusals [...]}`\n   150\t   naming each missing, malformed or not-exclusive option. A refusal publishes\n   151\t   nothing and mints nothing: the mirror's cursor is minted through the\n   152\t   channel reader only after every option passes, and a reader that\n   153\t   will not mint it refuses too.\"\n   154\t  [opts]\n   155\t  (let [rs (refusals opts)]\n   156\t    (if (seq rs)\n   157\t      {::status ::refused, ::refusals rs}\n   158\t      (let [end (::channel opts)\n   159\t            c (stream/cursor (:reader end) :dao.stream/oldest)]\n   160\t        (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome c))\n   161\t          {::status ::refused,\n   162\t           ::refusals [{::option ::channel, ::reason ::no-cursor,\n   163\t                        ::outcome c}]}\n   164\t          {::policy (merge {::codec ucf.remote/cursor-codec}\n   165\t                           (select-keys opts [::surface ::admit? ::capacity\n   166\t                                              ::step-budget ::codec]))\n   167\t           ::channel end\n   168\t           ::channel-descriptor (::channel-descriptor opts)\n   169\t           ::state (atom {:registry []\n   170\t                          :table {}\n   171\t                          :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor c)\n   172\t                          :closed? false})})))))\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\t;; =============================================================================\n   176\t;; The registry\n   177\t;; =============================================================================\n   178\t\n   179\t(defn- live-entry\n   180\t  \"The live registry entry for `h`, by reference identity.\"\n   181\t  [state h]\n   182\t  (some #(when (and (identical? h (:handle %)) (= :live (:status %))) %)\n   183\t        (:registry state)))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- live-count\n   187\t  [state]\n   188\t  (count (filter #(= :live (:status %)) (:registry state))))\n   189\t\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn- round-trips?\n   192\t  \"True when cursor `c` survives `codec` -- encoded, decoded back, and\n   193\t   equal: the rule `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s lift applies to a kept cursor,\n   194\t   plain data in the channel's portable domain.\"\n   195\t  [codec c]\n   196\t  (try (= c ((:decode codec) ((:encode codec) c)))\n   197\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false)))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn- portable-cursors?\n   201\t  \"True when `h`'s cursors survive the channel codec: the cursor it\n   202\t   mints at each standard anchor answers ok and round-trips. A handle\n   203\t   whose cursors hold a host object cannot be served, and is never\n   204\t   entered into the table (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3).\"\n   205\t  [codec h]\n   206\t  (every? (fn [anchor]\n   207\t            (let [r (stream/cursor h anchor)]\n   208\t              (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   209\t                   (round-trips? codec (:dao.stream/cursor r)))))\n   210\t          [:dao.stream/oldest :dao.stream/newest]))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn- servable-surface\n   214\t  \"The surface policy's answer for `h` when it is a non-empty subset of\n   215\t   `surfaces` that `h` itself implements and `h` answers descriptor --\n   216\t   the mirror answers descriptor from the handle directly -- and, for a\n   217\t   reader, when its cursors are portable; else nil.\"\n   218\t  [policy h]\n   219\t  (let [s ((::surface policy) h)]\n   220\t    (when (and (set? s)\n   221\t               (seq s)\n   222\t               (every? surfaces s)\n   223\t               (stream/descriptor? h)\n   224\t               (or (not (contains? s :reader))\n   225\t                   (and (stream/reader? h)\n   226\t                        (portable-cursors? (::codec policy) h)))\n   227\t               (or (not (contains? s :writer)) (stream/writer? h)))\n   228\t      s)))\n   229\t\n   230\t\n   231\t(defn- served\n   232\t  [entry]\n   233\t  {:dao.stream/identity (:identity entry)\n   234\t   :dao.stream/channel (:channel entry)})\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\t(defn table\n   238\t  \"The published table as the mirror reads it: `{served-identity\n   239\t   {:handle h :surface S}}` (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3). A snapshot,\n   240\t   plain data; retiring an identity removes it here first.\"\n   241\t  [binding]\n   242\t  (:table @(::state binding)))\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn entries\n   246\t  \"The registry's entries, oldest first: each `{:handle h :identity id\n   247\t   :channel cd :surface S :status s}`.\"\n   248\t  [binding]\n   249\t  (:registry @(::state binding)))\n   250\t\n   251\t\n   252\t(defn serve!\n   253\t  \"The UCF `serve!` callback (`yin.vm.ucf.remote`): `handle ->\n   254\t   {:dao.stream/identity id :dao.stream/channel descriptor}`, or nil\n   255\t   when this binding cannot serve `handle` -- the binding is closed,\n   256\t   the authority gate refuses, the surface policy refuses or names a\n   257\t   surface the handle lacks, or the capacity of live exports is\n   258\t   reached. A handle already live in this binding returns its one\n   259\t   identity and channel, with no second entry. A newly served handle\n   260\t   gets a freshly minted identity, never one this binding or any\n   261\t   other has used.\"\n   262\t  [binding handle]\n   263\t  (let [state (::state binding)\n   264\t        policy (::policy binding)\n   265\t        s @state]\n   266\t    (when-not (:closed? s)\n   267\t      (if-some [e (live-entry s handle)]\n   268\t        (served e)\n   269\t        (when-let [surface (and ((::admit? policy) handle)\n   270\t                                (servable-surface policy handle))]\n   271\t          (when (< (live-count s) (::capacity policy))\n   272\t            (let [e {:handle handle\n   273\t                     :identity (str (random-uuid))\n   274\t                     :channel (::channel-descriptor binding)\n   275\t                     :surface surface\n   276\t                     :status :live}]\n   277\t              (swap! state\n   278\t                     #(-> %\n   279\t                          (update :registry conj e)\n   280\t                          (assoc-in [:table (:identity e)]\n   281\t                                    {:handle handle :surface surface})))\n   282\t              (served e))))))))\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\t(defn serve-fn\n   286\t  \"`serve!` closed over `binding`, the one-argument shape\n   287\t   `yin.vm.ucf.remote` takes.\"\n   288\t  [binding]\n   289\t  (fn [handle] (serve! binding handle)))\n   290\t\n   291\t\n   292\t;; =============================================================================\n   293\t;; Retirement\n   294\t;; =============================================================================\n   295\t\n   296\t(defn retire!\n   297\t  \"The one retirement transition for served identity `identity`. First\n   298\t   the identity leaves the published table, so any later mirror step\n   299\t   answers a remote operation on it not-found; only then is its entry\n   300\t   released from the registry. Idempotent: an identity not live in this\n   301\t   binding -- already retired, or never served here -- retires nothing.\n   302\t   Returns `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok ::retired? bool}`.\"\n   303\t  [binding identity]\n   304\t  (let [state (::state binding)\n   305\t        live? (some #(and (= identity (:identity %)) (= :live (:status %)))\n   306\t                    (:registry @state))]\n   307\t    (when live?\n   308\t      ;; unpublish: no mirror step after this line can reach the handle\n   309\t      (swap! state\n   310\t             (fn [s]\n   311\t               (-> s\n   312\t                   (update :table dissoc identity)\n   313\t                   (update :registry\n   314\t                           (fn [r]\n   315\t                             (mapv #(if (= identity (:identity %))\n   316\t                                      (assoc % :status :retiring)\n   317\t                                      %)\n   318\t                                   r))))))\n   319\t      ;; release: the entry lets go of its handle\n   320\t      (swap! state update :registry\n   321\t             (fn [r] (filterv #(not= identity (:identity %)) r))))\n   322\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   323\t     ::retired? (boolean live?)}))\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\t(defn close!\n   327\t  \"Retire every live entry, then close the channel writer when it is\n   328\t   closable: the remote peer's channel reader answers end, and its link\n   329\t   reports every append! still outstanding as append-unknown -- the\n   330\t   transport's own close/loss path, nothing settled silently. Closing\n   331\t   the writer is the binding's to do only because of the ownership\n   332\t   contract `open!` required (::channel-exclusive?): the channel end is\n   333\t   dedicated to this binding, so no other reflection or mirror loses\n   334\t   its channel with it. Idempotent; afterwards `serve!` answers nil and `step` answers\n   335\t   closed.\"\n   336\t  [binding]\n   337\t  (let [state (::state binding)]\n   338\t    (when-not (:closed? @state)\n   339\t      (swap! state assoc :closed? true)\n   340\t      (doseq [e (:registry @state)]\n   341\t        (retire! binding (:identity e)))\n   342\t      (let [w (:writer (::channel binding))]\n   343\t        (when (stream/closable? w)\n   344\t          (stream/close! w))))\n   345\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))\n   346\t\n   347\t\n   348\t;; =============================================================================\n   349\t;; The drive\n   350\t;; =============================================================================\n   351\t\n   352\t(defn- budgeted-reader\n   353\t  \"A view of channel reader `r` that passes at most `budget` next calls\n   354\t   through to `r` and answers blocked, without reading, once they are\n   355\t   spent. Every outcome passed through is `r`'s own, verbatim, and the\n   356\t   view never constructs or rewrites a cursor, so the mirror holds\n   357\t   exactly the successor of the last value it read: blocked leaves it\n   358\t   there, and the next pass resumes from it. descriptor and cursor are\n   359\t   `r`'s own.\"\n   360\t  [r budget]\n   361\t  (let [left (volatile! budget)]\n   362\t    (reify\n   363\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   364\t\n   365\t      (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor r))\n   366\t\n   367\t\n   368\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   369\t\n   370\t      (cursor [_ anchor] (stream/cursor r anchor))\n   371\t\n   372\t      (next\n   373\t        [_ c]\n   374\t        (if (pos? @left)\n   375\t          (do (vswap! left dec)\n   376\t              (stream/next r c))\n   377\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))))\n   378\t\n   379\t\n   380\t(defn step\n   381\t  \"One bounded drive pass: one `dao.stream.remote/mirror-step` against\n   382\t   one snapshot of the published table, from the binding's own mirror\n   383\t   cursor, over at most `::step-budget` reads of the channel reader.\n   384\t   The pass ends where the channel answers blocked or end, or where the\n   385\t   budget is spent; either way the binding keeps the successor of the\n   386\t   last value read, and the next step resumes there -- nothing skipped,\n   387\t   nothing answered twice. Returns `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   388\t   ::advanced? bool}`, or `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}`\n   389\t   once closed. Like serve!, retire! and close!, step belongs to the\n   390\t   binding's one serialized drive owner: its read and write of the\n   391\t   state cell are not atomic against a concurrent caller.\"\n   392\t  [binding]\n   393\t  (let [state (::state binding)\n   394\t        s @state]\n   395\t    (if (:closed? s)\n   396\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}\n   397\t      (let [end (::channel binding)\n   398\t            c (:cursor s)\n   399\t            reader (budgeted-reader (:reader end)\n   400\t                                    (::step-budget (::policy binding)))\n   401\t            c' (remote/mirror-step (:table s) reader c (:writer end))]\n   402\t        (swap! state assoc :cursor c')\n   403\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   404\t         ::advanced? (not= c c')}))))\n   405\t\n   406\t\n   407\t;; =============================================================================\n   408\t;; Frame lift with refusal cleanup\n   409\t;; =============================================================================\n   410\t\n   411\t(defn lift-frame\n   412\t  \"`yin.vm.ucf.remote/lift-frame` with this binding's `serve!`, and\n   413\t   the cleanup a refused whole-frame lift needs: every identity the\n   414\t   lift itself minted is retired when the frame refuses, so no\n   415\t   provisional export outlives a lift that published nothing. Handles\n   416\t   already served before the lift stay served.\"\n   417\t  ([binding resources pending]\n   418\t   (lift-frame binding resources pending (::codec (::policy binding))))\n   419\t  ([binding resources pending codec]\n   420\t   (let [before (into #{} (map :identity) (entries binding))\n   421\t         r (ucf.remote/lift-frame (serve-fn binding) resources pending codec)]\n   422\t     (when (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   423\t       (doseq [e (entries binding)]\n   424\t         (when-not (contains? before (:identity e))\n   425\t           (retire! binding (:identity e)))))\n   426\t     r)))\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve-test\n     2\t  \"Slice 3a, the FFI export binding: open! refuses an incomplete\n     3\t   assembly before anything is published; serve! is stable per live\n     4\t   handle by reference identity -- the two serve! calls lift-frame makes\n     5\t   for one handle yield one identity and one table entry -- and refuses\n     6\t   what the gate, the surface policy, the capacity or a closed binding\n     7\t   refuses; retire! unpublishes first, is idempotent, and a re-served\n     8\t   handle gets a new identity while the old one answers not-found;\n     9\t   close! retires everything and a remote peer's unresolved append ends\n    10\t   as append-unknown; a refused whole-frame lift leaves no provisional\n    11\t   export behind.\"\n    12\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    13\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    14\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    15\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    16\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    17\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    18\t            [yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve :as rs]\n    19\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t;; =============================================================================\n    23\t;; The toy: two in-process ring buffers as the channel (as\n    24\t;; dao.stream.remote-test); the binding is peer B\n    25\t;; =============================================================================\n    26\t\n    27\t(defn- ring\n    28\t  [capacity]\n    29\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    30\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    31\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t(def ^:private chan\n    35\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    36\t   :dao.stream/identity \"remote-serve-toy\"})\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- toy\n    40\t  []\n    41\t  (let [ab (ring 64)\n    42\t        ba (ring 64)]\n    43\t    {:ab ab, :ba ba,\n    44\t     :a-end {:reader ba, :writer ab},\n    45\t     :b-end {:reader ab, :writer ba}}))\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn- opts\n    49\t  \"A complete assembly over `t`'s B end, declared exclusive to the\n    50\t   binding: every handle admitted, served with `surface`, at most\n    51\t   `capacity` live exports.\"\n    52\t  ([t] (opts t (constantly #{:reader :writer}) 8))\n    53\t  ([t surface capacity]\n    54\t   {::rs/channel (:b-end t)\n    55\t    ::rs/channel-exclusive? true\n    56\t    ::rs/channel-descriptor chan\n    57\t    ::rs/surface surface\n    58\t    ::rs/admit? (constantly true)\n    59\t    ::rs/capacity capacity\n    60\t    ::rs/step-budget 64}))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn- values\n    64\t  [h]\n    65\t  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n    66\t         acc []]\n    67\t    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n    68\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    69\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n    70\t        acc))))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn- ask\n    74\t  \"Put one raw wire request for `identity` on A's side, run one binding\n    75\t   step, and return the answer carrying `id` from B's answers.\"\n    76\t  [t b identity id op args]\n    77\t  (stream/append! (:ab t) {:dao.stream/identity identity\n    78\t                           :dao.stream.remote/op op\n    79\t                           :dao.stream.remote/args args\n    80\t                           :dao.stream.remote/id id})\n    81\t  (rs/step b)\n    82\t  (some #(when (= id (:dao.stream.remote/id %)) %) (values (:ba t))))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(defrecord ValueHandle\n    86\t  [id]\n    87\t\n    88\t  stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n    89\t\n    90\t  (descriptor\n    91\t    [_]\n    92\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    93\t     :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/value\n    94\t                             :dao.stream/identity id}\n    95\t     :dao.stream/identity id})\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    99\t\n   100\t  (cursor [_ _] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t  (next [_ _] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t;; the retained call's frame: call-in is written by the remote retry,\n   107\t;; call-out read at the kept response cursor -- the frame whose lift\n   108\t;; asks serve! for call-out twice (the response marker, then its cell)\n   109\t(defn- retained-resources\n   110\t  [call-in call-out]\n   111\t  {vm/call-in-stream-key call-in,\n   112\t   vm/call-out-stream-key call-out,\n   113\t   vm/call-out-cursor-key\n   114\t   {:stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   115\t    :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor call-out :dao.stream/oldest))}})\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(def ^:private retained-entry\n   119\t  {:reason :put, :request-sent true, :call-id :call-7,\n   120\t   :op :op/add, :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key,\n   121\t   :datom (assoc (apply2/request :call-7 :op/add [1 2])\n   122\t                 :producer/nonce \"n-1\")})\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn- call-pair-surface\n   126\t  [call-in]\n   127\t  (fn [h] (if (identical? h call-in) #{:writer} #{:reader})))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t;; =============================================================================\n   131\t;; Assembly\n   132\t;; =============================================================================\n   133\t\n   134\t(deftest open-refuses-an-incomplete-assembly\n   135\t  (let [t (toy)\n   136\t        full (opts t)]\n   137\t    (is (rs/binding? (rs/open! full)))\n   138\t    (doseq [k [::rs/channel ::rs/channel-exclusive? ::rs/channel-descriptor\n   139\t               ::rs/surface ::rs/admit? ::rs/capacity ::rs/step-budget]]\n   140\t      (testing (str \"without \" k)\n   141\t        (let [r (rs/open! (dissoc full k))]\n   142\t          (is (= ::rs/refused (::rs/status r)))\n   143\t          (is (= [{::rs/option k, ::rs/reason ::rs/missing}]\n   144\t                 (::rs/refusals r)))\n   145\t          (is (not (rs/binding? r)) \"nothing to serve through\"))))\n   146\t    (testing \"exclusivity is a declaration: anything but true refuses\"\n   147\t      (doseq [v [false nil :yes 1]]\n   148\t        (is (= [{::rs/option ::rs/channel-exclusive?,\n   149\t                 ::rs/reason ::rs/not-exclusive}]\n   150\t               (::rs/refusals\n   151\t                 (rs/open! (assoc full ::rs/channel-exclusive? v)))))))\n   152\t    (testing \"the authority gate has no default: nil is malformed\"\n   153\t      (is (= [{::rs/option ::rs/admit?, ::rs/reason ::rs/malformed}]\n   154\t             (::rs/refusals (rs/open! (assoc full ::rs/admit? nil))))))\n   155\t    (testing \"a capacity that is not a positive integer\"\n   156\t      (is (= [{::rs/option ::rs/capacity, ::rs/reason ::rs/malformed}]\n   157\t             (::rs/refusals (rs/open! (assoc full ::rs/capacity 0))))))\n   158\t    (testing \"a step budget that is not a positive integer: no unbounded\n   159\t              pass\"\n   160\t      (is (= [{::rs/option ::rs/step-budget, ::rs/reason ::rs/malformed}]\n   161\t             (::rs/refusals (rs/open! (assoc full ::rs/step-budget nil))))))\n   162\t    (testing \"a codec, when given, must be {:encode f :decode f}\"\n   163\t      (is (= [{::rs/option ::rs/codec, ::rs/reason ::rs/malformed}]\n   164\t             (::rs/refusals (rs/open! (assoc full ::rs/codec {}))))))\n   165\t    (testing \"a channel end without a reader\"\n   166\t      (is (= ::rs/malformed\n   167\t             (-> (rs/open! (assoc full ::rs/channel {:writer (:ab t)}))\n   168\t                 ::rs/refusals first ::rs/reason))))\n   169\t    (testing \"a refusal wrote nothing toward the peer\"\n   170\t      (is (empty? (values (:ba t)))))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t;; =============================================================================\n   174\t;; serve! idempotence\n   175\t;; =============================================================================\n   176\t\n   177\t(deftest serve-is-stable-per-live-handle\n   178\t  (let [t (toy)\n   179\t        b (rs/open! (opts t))\n   180\t        h (ring 4)\n   181\t        s1 (rs/serve! b h)\n   182\t        s2 (rs/serve! b h)]\n   183\t    (is (= chan (:dao.stream/channel s1)))\n   184\t    (is (= s1 s2) \"the identical identity and channel\")\n   185\t    (is (= 1 (count (rs/table b))) \"one table entry\")\n   186\t    (is (= {:handle h, :surface #{:reader :writer}}\n   187\t           (get (rs/table b) (:dao.stream/identity s1)))\n   188\t        \"the mirror's plain table shape\")\n   189\t    (testing \"keyed by reference identity, not equality\"\n   190\t      (let [v1 (->ValueHandle \"same\")\n   191\t            v2 (->ValueHandle \"same\")\n   192\t            b' (rs/open! (opts t (constantly #{:reader}) 8))]\n   193\t        (is (= v1 v2))\n   194\t        (is (not= (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b' v1))\n   195\t                  (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b' v2))))\n   196\t        (is (= 2 (count (rs/table b'))))))))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(deftest lift-frame-serves-one-handle-once-across-both-call-sites\n   200\t  (let [t (toy)\n   201\t        call-in (ring 4)\n   202\t        call-out (ring 4)\n   203\t        b (rs/open! (opts t (call-pair-surface call-in) 8))\n   204\t        calls (atom [])\n   205\t        serve! (fn [h] (swap! calls conj h) (rs/serve! b h))\n   206\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve!\n   207\t                                      (retained-resources call-in call-out)\n   208\t                                      [retained-entry])\n   209\t        pending (first (:yin.k/pending lifted))\n   210\t        cell-marker (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/response-cell pending)\n   211\t                                    :yin.k/stream])]\n   212\t    (is (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending)))\n   213\t    (is (< 1 (count (filter #(identical? call-out %) @calls)))\n   214\t        \"lift-frame asked for call-out from lift-one and from mint-cell\")\n   215\t    (is (= (:yin.k/response pending) cell-marker)\n   216\t        \"identical markers: identity and channel\")\n   217\t    (is (= 2 (count (rs/table b)))\n   218\t        \"one entry for call-in, one for call-out\")\n   219\t    (is (= 1 (count (filter #(identical? call-out (:handle %))\n   220\t                            (vals (rs/table b))))))\n   221\t    (is (= #{:writer}\n   222\t           (get-in (rs/table b) [(get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   223\t                                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   224\t                                 :surface]))\n   225\t        \"the declared surface the policy gave\")))\n   226\t\n   227\t\n   228\t;; =============================================================================\n   229\t;; Retirement\n   230\t;; =============================================================================\n   231\t\n   232\t(deftest retire-unpublishes-and-never-reuses-an-identity\n   233\t  (let [t (toy)\n   234\t        b (rs/open! (opts t))\n   235\t        h (ring 4)\n   236\t        _ (stream/append! h :v)\n   237\t        id (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b h))]\n   238\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   239\t           (:dao.stream/outcome\n   240\t             (ask t b id 0 :dao.stream/cursor [:dao.stream/oldest])))\n   241\t        \"served: the mirror answers from the handle\")\n   242\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, ::rs/retired? true}\n   243\t           (rs/retire! b id)))\n   244\t    (is (not (contains? (rs/table b) id)) \"unpublished\")\n   245\t    (is (empty? (rs/entries b)) \"and released\")\n   246\t    (is (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   247\t           (:dao.stream.remote/error\n   248\t             (ask t b id 1 :dao.stream/cursor [:dao.stream/oldest])))\n   249\t        \"a remote op on the retired identity answers not-found\")\n   250\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, ::rs/retired? false}\n   251\t           (rs/retire! b id))\n   252\t        \"idempotent\")\n   253\t    (let [id' (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b h))]\n   254\t      (is (some? id'))\n   255\t      (is (not= id id') \"re-served under a NEW identity\")\n   256\t      (is (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   257\t             (:dao.stream.remote/error\n   258\t               (ask t b id 2 :dao.stream/next [0])))\n   259\t          \"the old identity stays not-found\")\n   260\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   261\t             (:dao.stream/outcome\n   262\t               (ask t b id' 3 :dao.stream/cursor [:dao.stream/oldest])))))))\n   263\t\n   264\t\n   265\t(deftest close-retires-everything\n   266\t  (let [t (toy)\n   267\t        b (rs/open! (opts t))\n   268\t        ids (mapv #(:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b %)) [(ring 2) (ring 2)])]\n   269\t    (is (= 2 (count (rs/table b))))\n   270\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok} (rs/close! b)))\n   271\t    (is (empty? (rs/table b)))\n   272\t    (is (empty? (rs/entries b)))\n   273\t    (is (nil? (rs/serve! b (ring 2))) \"a closed binding serves nothing\")\n   274\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed} (rs/step b)))\n   275\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok} (rs/close! b)) \"idempotent\")\n   276\t    (is (every? #(false? (::rs/retired? (rs/retire! b %))) ids))))\n   277\t\n   278\t\n   279\t(deftest an-unresolved-remote-append-ends-as-append-unknown\n   280\t  (let [t (toy)\n   281\t        o (opts t (constantly #{:writer}) 8)\n   282\t        b (rs/open! o)\n   283\t        target (ring 4)\n   284\t        id (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b target))\n   285\t        events (ring 16)\n   286\t        attach! (remote/attacher {:dao.stream.remote/channels {chan (:a-end t)}\n   287\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/events events})\n   288\t        refl (:dao.stream/handle\n   289\t               (attach! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   290\t                         :dao.stream/identity id\n   291\t                         :dao.stream/channel chan}))]\n   292\t    (rs/step b)\n   293\t    (stream/descriptor refl)\n   294\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! refl :x)))\n   295\t        \"accepted on the outbound path, unanswered: no step ran\")\n   296\t    (is (true? (::rs/channel-exclusive? o))\n   297\t        \"the binding owns its channel end by declaration\")\n   298\t    (rs/close! b)\n   299\t    (is (= :dao.stream/closed\n   300\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! (:ba t) :after)))\n   301\t        \"close! closed the binding's own channel writer\")\n   302\t    (stream/descriptor refl)\n   303\t    (let [unknown (filter #(= :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   304\t                              (:dao.stream.remote/event %))\n   305\t                          (values events))]\n   306\t      (is (= 1 (count unknown))\n   307\t          \"the channel's end runs the loss path: append-unknown\"))\n   308\t    (is (empty? (values target)) \"the request never reached the mirror\")))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t;; =============================================================================\n   312\t;; Refusal\n   313\t;; =============================================================================\n   314\t\n   315\t(deftest step-is-a-bounded-pass\n   316\t  (let [t (toy)\n   317\t        b (rs/open! (assoc (opts t) ::rs/step-budget 2))\n   318\t        id (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b (ring 4)))\n   319\t        answered (fn []\n   320\t                   (mapv :dao.stream.remote/id\n   321\t                         (filter #(contains? % :dao.stream.remote/id)\n   322\t                                 (values (:ba t)))))]\n   323\t    (doseq [n (range 5)]\n   324\t      (stream/append! (:ab t) {:dao.stream/identity id\n   325\t                               :dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   326\t                               :dao.stream.remote/args [:dao.stream/oldest]\n   327\t                               :dao.stream.remote/id n}))\n   328\t    (is (true? (::rs/advanced? (rs/step b))))\n   329\t    (is (= [0 1] (answered)) \"exactly the budget, in order\")\n   330\t    (rs/step b)\n   331\t    (is (= [0 1 2 3] (answered)) \"resumed from the kept successor\")\n   332\t    (rs/step b)\n   333\t    (is (= [0 1 2 3 4] (answered)))\n   334\t    (is (false? (::rs/advanced? (rs/step b))) \"the channel is blocked\")\n   335\t    (is (= [0 1 2 3 4] (answered)) \"nothing skipped, nothing answered twice\")))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t(defn- host-cursor-reader\n   339\t  \"A served reader whose cursors hold a host object -- a function --\n   340\t   which no channel codec carries.\"\n   341\t  []\n   342\t  (let [host (fn [])]\n   343\t    (reify\n   344\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   345\t\n   346\t      (descriptor\n   347\t        [_]\n   348\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   349\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/host\n   350\t                                 :dao.stream/identity \"host\"}\n   351\t         :dao.stream/identity \"host\"})\n   352\t\n   353\t\n   354\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   355\t\n   356\t      (cursor\n   357\t        [_ _]\n   358\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   359\t         :dao.stream/cursor {:at host}})\n   360\t\n   361\t      (next [_ _] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n   362\t\n   363\t\n   364\t(deftest a-reader-whose-cursors-are-not-portable-is-never-entered\n   365\t  (let [t (toy)]\n   366\t    (testing \"a host object in the cursor\"\n   367\t      (let [b (rs/open! (opts t (constantly #{:reader}) 8))]\n   368\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b (host-cursor-reader))))\n   369\t        (is (empty? (rs/table b)))\n   370\t        (is (empty? (rs/entries b)))))\n   371\t    (testing \"a writer-only surface names no cursors\"\n   372\t      (let [b (rs/open! (opts t (constantly #{:writer}) 8))]\n   373\t        (is (some? (rs/serve! b (ring 2))))))\n   374\t    (testing \"the binding's own codec judges\"\n   375\t      (let [refusing {:encode (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"uncarried\" {})))\n   376\t                      :decode identity}\n   377\t            b (rs/open! (assoc (opts t (constantly #{:reader}) 8)\n   378\t                               ::rs/codec refusing))]\n   379\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b (ring 2))))\n   380\t        (is (empty? (rs/table b)))))))\n   381\t\n   382\t\n   383\t(deftest serve-refuses-what-policy-refuses\n   384\t  (let [t (toy)\n   385\t        h (ring 2)]\n   386\t    (testing \"the authority gate\"\n   387\t      (let [b (rs/open! (assoc (opts t) ::rs/admit? (constantly false)))]\n   388\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b h)))\n   389\t        (is (empty? (rs/table b)))))\n   390\t    (testing \"the surface policy\"\n   391\t      (let [b (rs/open! (opts t (constantly nil) 8))]\n   392\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b h))))\n   393\t      (let [b (rs/open! (opts t (constantly #{:closable}) 8))]\n   394\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b h)) \"not a served surface\")))\n   395\t    (testing \"a surface the handle does not implement\"\n   396\t      (let [b (rs/open! (opts t (constantly #{:writer}) 8))]\n   397\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b (->ValueHandle \"r\"))))))\n   398\t    (testing \"the capacity of live exports\"\n   399\t      (let [b (rs/open! (opts t (constantly #{:reader}) 1))\n   400\t            first-id (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b h))]\n   401\t        (is (nil? (rs/serve! b (ring 2))))\n   402\t        (is (some? (rs/serve! b h)) \"a live handle is still answered\")\n   403\t        (rs/retire! b first-id)\n   404\t        (is (some? (rs/serve! b (ring 2))) \"retirement frees capacity\")))))\n   405\t\n   406\t\n   407\t(deftest a-refused-frame-leaves-no-provisional-export\n   408\t  (let [t (toy)\n   409\t        call-in (ring 4)\n   410\t        call-out (ring 4)\n   411\t        b (rs/open! (assoc (opts t (call-pair-surface call-in) 8)\n   412\t                           ::rs/admit? #(not (identical? call-out %))))\n   413\t        r (rs/lift-frame b (retained-resources call-in call-out)\n   414\t                         [retained-entry])]\n   415\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status r)))\n   416\t    (is (not (contains? r :yin.k/pending)) \"no lift is published\")\n   417\t    (is (empty? (rs/table b))\n   418\t        \"call-in, served before call-out refused, was retired\")\n   419\t    (is (empty? (rs/entries b))))\n   420\t  (testing \"a handle served before the lift stays served\"\n   421\t    (let [t (toy)\n   422\t          call-in (ring 4)\n   423\t          call-out (ring 4)\n   424\t          b (rs/open! (assoc (opts t (call-pair-surface call-in) 8)\n   425\t                             ::rs/admit? #(not (identical? call-out %))))\n   426\t          id (:dao.stream/identity (rs/serve! b call-in))]\n   427\t      (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied\n   428\t             (:yin.k/status\n   429\t               (rs/lift-frame b (retained-resources call-in call-out)\n   430\t                              [retained-entry]))))\n   431\t      (is (= [id] (keys (rs/table b)))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
